			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement registry-backed vscode.comments namespace shim\n\nThe stock inline stub in EnsureVscodeAPI.ts for `vscode.comments` used empty no-op objects whose `createCommentController` returned a stateless shell where every `createCommentThread` call produced a fresh thread that silently dropped metadata. Extensions like GitHub Pull Requests and GitLens call `controller.createCommentThread(uri, range, comments)` on activation and later dereference the thread's `.comments`, `.state`, or `.label` — with the stub, those reads always returned undefined.\n\nReplace the stub with a dynamic import of a registry-backed `CommentsNamespace` factory in Source/Services/Handler/VscodeAPI/Comments/Namespace.ts. Each CommentController owns a `Map`-backed thread registry keyed on `UriStr:Line:Char`, with mutable thread state for comments, collapsibleState, canReply, contextValue, label, and state. Registration is idempotent — re-registration returns the existing instance, softening VS Code's duplicate-id throw.\n\nAlso regenerate RouteManifest to add three newly exposed Mountain RPC methods (`setStatusBarText`, `Task.Terminate`, `terminate_task`), bringing the count from 137 to 140.\n\nReal comment-pane UI rendering (gutter markers, inline balloons) requires Sky-side `ICommentService` exposure and remains deferred (Mountain-Crate-Split.md §#7b). The shim keeps the extension's internal thread list coherent so commenting workflows that emit notifications or track reaction handlers work end-to-end inside the extension host.",
			"SHA": "e5b2a278b9ad980d7e49b9cfcd333bc0d00fa7e1"
		}
	],
